### Way 1: HTTP client interceptor (domain tool on a RestClient with the payments interceptor)

POST http://localhost:8080/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: example-session-0000000000000001

{ "prompt" : "Give me a short recap of recent prediction-market activity.", "approach" : "interceptor" }


### Way 2: paidHttpRequest tool (generic fetch tool, URL in the prompt)

POST http://localhost:8080/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: example-session-0000000000000001

{ "prompt" : "Fetch https://sandbox.node4all.com/v1/x402-test and summarize it in one sentence. Then tell me the remaining budget of my payment session.", "approach" : "tool" }


### Way 3: own integration (domain tool on the JDK HttpClient paying through AgentCorePaymentsTemplate)

POST http://localhost:8080/invocations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amzn-Bedrock-AgentCore-Runtime-Session-Id: example-session-0000000000000001

{ "prompt" : "Read my fortune, in one sentence.", "approach" : "custom" }
